{
  "id": "29380_uritsukeru",
  "headword": "{売|う}りつける",
  "reading": "うりつける",
  "romaji": "uritsukeru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to force a sale on; to palm off; to foist on",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to force a sale on someone; to palm off; to foist on",
      "explanation": "To pressure someone into buying something, often something overpriced, unneeded, or of poor quality. The buyer is marked with に and the goods with を."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29380_uritsukeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{高|たか}い{壺|つぼ}を{売|う}りつける。",
      "english": "to foist an expensive vase on someone",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29380_uritsukeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{老人|ろうじん}に{不要|ふよう}な{商品|しょうひん}を{売|う}りつけた。",
      "english": "They palmed off unnecessary goods on an elderly person.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29380_uritsukeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{言葉巧|ことばたく}みに、{客|きゃく}に{高額|こうがく}な{保険|ほけん}を{売|う}りつける{業者|ぎょうしゃ}もいる。",
      "english": "Some dealers smooth-talk customers into buying expensive insurance.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). The buyer is marked with に and the goods with を. Compound of {売|う}る (to sell) + つける.\n\nUSAGE:\nCarries a negative nuance — it implies a pushy, one-sided sale of something the buyer did not really want.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {無理|むり}やり{売|う}りつける: to force a sale on someone\n- {高値|たかね}で{売|う}りつける: to palm off at an inflated price",
